{"comment_text": {"ja76:0.1": "", "ja76:0.2": "", "ja76:0.3": "", "ja76:0.4": "", "ja76:1.1": "An ascetic is unafraid even in the presence of bandits, for he has nothing to lose. ", "ja76:1.2": "", "ja76:1.3": "For this idiom, see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn12/en/sujato#39.7'>MN 12:39.7</a>. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Samārūḷha</i> is literally “mounted”; the expression refers to travelling along on a horse, etc. ", "ja76:1.4": "", "ja76:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja76:0.1": "<article id='ja76'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja76:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja76:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja76:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja76:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja76:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja76:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja76:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja76:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja76:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja76:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja76:0.3": "Varuṇavagga ", "ja76:0.4": "6. Asaṅkiyajātaka ", "ja76:1.1": "“Asaṅkiyomhi gāmamhi, ", "ja76:1.2": "araññe natthi me bhayaṁ; ", "ja76:1.3": "Ujuṁ maggaṁ samārūḷho, ", "ja76:1.4": "mettāya karuṇāya cā”ti. ", "ja76:2.1": "Asaṅkiyajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja76:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 76 ", "ja76:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja76:0.3": "The Warding Tree ", "ja76:0.4": "Unsuspecting: a past life story ", "ja76:1.1": "I am unsuspecting in the village; ", "ja76:1.2": "in the wilderness there’s no peril for me: ", "ja76:1.3": "I ride upon the straight path ", "ja76:1.4": "with love and compassion. ", "ja76:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja76:0.1": "", "ja76:0.2": "", "ja76:0.3": "", "ja76:0.4": "", "ja76:1.1": "ms22J_167, msdiv76, pts-vp-pli1.334", "ja76:1.2": "", "ja76:1.3": "", "ja76:1.4": "", "ja76:2.1": "ms22J_168"}, "keys_order": ["ja76:0.1", "ja76:0.2", "ja76:0.3", "ja76:0.4", "ja76:1.1", "ja76:1.2", "ja76:1.3", "ja76:1.4", "ja76:2.1"]}